docs/plans/
# Most plan-loop machinery under docs/scripts/ is local tooling, but every file
# named by .github/workflows/ci.yml must exist in a fresh checkout, or the job
# fails on a clone that is missing them. That is the four repository boundary
# checks, check_lib.sh, which all four source, and the five files the shellcheck
# step lints: the shared cargo-output classifier, the two verification runners
# that source it, and the resolution and graph proof runners that source it and
# check_lib.sh. `shellcheck -x` follows those source directives, so a sourced
# helper left untracked fails the lint as surely as a missing subject would.
# Ignoring the directory itself would stop git descending into it, so the
# entries are ignored and the ten files re-included.
docs/scripts/*
!docs/scripts/cargo_infrastructure.sh
!docs/scripts/check_lang_feature_forwarding.sh
!docs/scripts/check_lib.sh
!docs/scripts/check_published_manifests.sh
!docs/scripts/check_syntax_capabilities.sh
!docs/scripts/check_syntax_dependency_closure.sh
!docs/scripts/run_graph_proof.sh
!docs/scripts/run_resolution_proof.sh
!docs/scripts/verify_affected.sh
!docs/scripts/verify_step.sh
docs/internal/
docs/planning_guidelines.md
docs/introspection_guidelines.md
docs/rust_profile.md
docs/design-rationale.md
docs/testing.md
.mcp.json
